vLLM (ROCm Kimi-K3.1 build, f5926fb) DSA batch invariance for Kimi-K3.1 under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1: the DSA
layers force sparse MQA and disable ShardQ; the indexer computes decode logits like prefill (row-bounded [ks, ke)
kernels) and selects top-k deterministically; sparse MLA decode runs with one KV split; the AITER FA MLA prefill and
the indexer backend accept batch-invariant mode for this model only. Applied to site-packages with patch -p1 -F0.
Upstream status: not yet proposed.

